                </paragraph>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="block">$$\sum\limits_{n = 2}^{\infty}\frac{n^{2} + n}{n^{3} - 2}\qquad\sum\limits_{n = 2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{n}$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
              <item>
                <paragraph>
                  Use the Limit Comparison Test to show that that the first series diverges by comparing it to the second series.
                </paragraph>
                <paragraph>
                  <math display="block">$$\sum\limits_{n = 2}^{\infty}\frac{n^{2} - n}{n^{3} + 2}\qquad\sum\limits_{n = 2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{n}$$</math>
                </paragraph>
              </item>
            </list>
          </statement>
        </problem>
        <problem number="5">
          <statement>
            <paragraph>
              Which of the following inequalities can be used to show that <math display="inline">$$\sum\limits_{n = 1}^{\infty}n/(n^{3} + 1)$$</math> converges?
